# - DancehallReggaeWorld, Chronic Law profile (opened 2026-10-20, article dated February 2019): birth name spelled Ackeme Campbell, from the small town of Yallahs on the east side of Jamaica, secondary education at Morant Bay High School; first recording in 2009, War Dem A Ask fah, produced by Sting G Music Ltd on the Cemetary Riddim; Stress Free in August 2018 with producer Romaine McFarlane on EastSyde Records; Government in September 2018, produced by Cashflow Rinse and KevStar Records, described as an instant hit; singles list Celebrate, Born Fi Diss, Never Stop Try, Circumstances, Born Killa, Hilltop Gyallis, Gyal and Gun, Money Hunter, Bless Me; Cyan Kool produced by Triple B Ent; member of the Montego Bay 6ix team headed by Squash. The same article also says he is from the parish of Portland, which contradicts its own Yallahs location and the St. Thomas attribution of Shazam and DancehallMag.
# - Kaboom Magazine, KKRYTICAL signs with Showtime Services (opened 2026-10-20, published August 6, 2026): KKRYTICAL, given name Ron Longmore, Jamaican born and New York based, earned recognition with Loyalty, Hustla, 7.62 and Asphalt featuring Chronic Law.
# - World Music Views, Chronic Law tag page (opened 2026-10-20): Empty overtook Skeng Protocol as the most streamed song on YouTube Jamaica of all time according to its data; Kick It Wid Myself by Popcaan and Chronic Law released January 3, 2025, described as an anthem for the youth of St. Thomas; Corrupt Pt3 (Not a Valentines) number one on the YouTube Jamaica chart for the week ending February 20, 2025, debuting with 250,632 streams; Chronic Law crowned most viewed artist in June 2025 coverage; Chronic Law holds number one on YouTube Jamaica for the week ending October 1, 2026.
# - Hunnypot Unlimited, review of Chronic Law and Notnice, I.C.E. (Inside, Cold, and Empty) (opened 2026-10-20): nine track project produced largely by Notnice, written after a 73 day detention in a US immigration facility; track by track account names Intro, Like Samson, Prayer Work, Tree Limb, the Call skit, Ride or Die, Pain Pt. 2, It s Hard and If A Neva God.
